Here's a better idea:

1) First, recall the following game mechanics concerning scrolls:

* You can "read" a scroll from memory while blind if you have learned
what the mystic runes on it are.
* The runes can be learned in two ways: one, by reading the scroll, and
two, by hearing a monster read a scroll.

2) Now that you've cogitated that, here's some changes:

* Make the Book of the Dead always be generated cursed.
* Make it so that the Wizard of Yendor can read the Book aloud (to
summon undead) as an attack.

3) Now, to ascend illiterate:

* At some point, hear the Wizard read from the Book.
* Go to the invocation space, and blindfold yourself.
* Attempt to "read" the Book while blind. You will "pronounce the
mystic runes" from memory without ever reading them.

There you go. Totally sensible.

But...! There is one significant problem to this otherwise succulent
plan:

BUG: If you read a scroll while blind, and you learned the scroll's
runes from hearing (a monster) rather than sight (reading), then you
_still_ violate illiterate conduct.



